WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.333 --> 00:00:05.500
Want to see how a number
was reached? Open Breakdown.

2
00:00:06.333 --> 00:00:09.600
Every calculation, step by step. Nothing hidden.

3
00:00:13.133 --> 00:00:15.600
Export a polished quotation for the trader.

4
00:00:17.333 --> 00:00:19.600
Your costs stay on a separate internal sheet.

5
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.067
Then he comes back, with his own rate.

6
00:00:27.533 --> 00:00:29.900
Before you reply, open Check an offer.

7
00:00:30.667 --> 00:00:32.800
Pick the costing, and type his rate.

8
00:00:38.333 --> 00:00:43.433
Here you keep forty-two paisa a metre: eight
thousand four hundred rupees on the order.

9
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:45.767
Now you know whether to say yes.

10
00:00:47.833 --> 00:00:51.233
Open Breakdown again. The
version rail keeps every one.

11
00:00:51.833 --> 00:00:54.800
Same quality, different yarn
rates, different costs.

12
00:00:55.167 --> 00:00:59.233
The latest is always on top, and
older versions keep their numbers.

13
00:00:59.833 --> 00:01:05.567
Haven't propagated yet? Saved Costings shows
which costings are behind today's rates.

14
00:01:06.167 --> 00:01:10.800
And archive the costings and yarns you
no longer use, to keep things tidy.
